---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BrandHeader from '../components/BrandHeader.astro';
import BrandFooter from '../components/BrandFooter.astro';
import { site } from '../content/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About the Portfolio Demos | GTP Special Occasion Websites"
  description="How Griffin Technology Partners' fictional website and client-portal demonstrations work, including privacy and customization details."
  canonicalPath="/about-the-demos"
>
  <BrandHeader />
  <main id="main-content" class="about-page">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">About this portfolio</p><h1>
        Real capabilities. Entirely fictional stories.
      </h1><p>
        These experiences help you see what a custom public website and customer administration area
        can feel like before your own story, content, and approved media are added.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <section>
        <span>01</span><h2>Nothing here is a customer story</h2><p>
          Every person, event, organization, RSVP, message, date, and detail is fictional. Licensed
          demonstration imagery does not depict GTP customers.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <span>02</span><h2>Portal edits stay in your browser</h2><p>
          The interactive previews use local browser storage. They do not submit information to GTP,
          Azure, or any third party. Reset clears the saved demonstration state.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <span>03</span><h2>Real administration is protected</h2><p>
          Customer portals are configured separately for approved users. This public portfolio
          deliberately includes no login form, credentials, backend, or customer data.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <span>04</span><h2>Your site will be your own</h2><p>
          These samples demonstrate breadth, not fixed templates. GTP adapts the structure, tone,
          typography, media, and management modules to the moment.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <section class="privacy-panel">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">A simple starting package</p><h2>{site.price} one time</h2><ul>
          {site.inclusions.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div><div>
        <p>
          Have an occasion in mind that is not shown here? The same approach can support launches,
          dedications, community milestones, and thoughtful surprises.
        </p><a class="button" href={site.offerUrl}>See the current offer</a><a
          class="text-link"
          href={`mailto:${site.salesEmail}`}>Ask a question by email</a
        >
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <BrandFooter />
</BaseLayout>
